---
// What rotli does, as one story in three steps (the owner, 2026-10-06: "clarify view vs where
// it actually lives … you write a note and open it in your view, Librarian puts it in vault
// accordingly, later ask AI about it and AI has indexing to get to it quick without wasting your
// tokens"). It also absorbed the former "You write for yourself. AI reads differently." section,
// whose before and after is now the File step's picture (the owner, the same day: the two were
// redundant). Each step is a heading and one or two sentences beside one picture drawn in HTML
// on the site's tokens, with the app's quokka standing on it; no outer cards (the owner,
// 2026-10-05):
//   1. Write: the note in your view and its one file in the vault (ViewAndVault.astro);
//   2. File: the Librarian's before and after, which plays once (Filing.astro);
//   3. Ask: a chat that searches on your computer and reads only what it found (AskIndex.astro).
// Every claim is a contract's (docs/design/landing-layout-2026-10-05.md lists them): views are
// reference projections, never stores, and a note's place in Main never follows its file
// (memex-data-contract.md, "One physical home, many views"); the Librarian is optional and
// Mac-only, moves files to wiki/<area>/ and writes only its declared fields, never the body
// ("Metadata ownership"); the AI searches locally and reads only selected notes, never the
// whole vault ("Master memory retrieval"); secure notes never reach a remote model
// (docs/design/ai-visibility-matrix.md).
// Under the steps, "What is an LLM wiki?" in two sentences, with Karpathy's gist as the source.
import AskIndex from './AskIndex.astro';
import Filing from './Filing.astro';
import ViewAndVault from './ViewAndVault.astro';

/** Andrej Karpathy's "LLM Wiki" gist (2026-04-04), the source of the term. */
const LLM_WIKI_SOURCE = 'https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f';
---

<section class="section overview" id="features" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="overview-title">Write it down. <span class="inked">rotli puts it away.</span></h2>
      <p class="section-lede">
        Where a note shows up and where its file lives are two different things. You arrange notes in a view.
        Each file lives once, in your vault: the folder you chose.
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step" data-reveal>
        <div class="step-copy">
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <h3>Write in your view</h3>
          <p>
            Start a note and keep it open in your view: Main, or a named view for a project. A view is your own
            arrangement of notes, never a copy of them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ViewAndVault />
      </li>

      <li class="step" data-reveal>
        <div class="step-copy">
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <h3>The Librarian files it</h3>
          <p>
            When it’s on, the Librarian later moves the file to its area folder in your vault and adds an area, a
            summary, tags, and links at the top. It never changes your words, and your view still shows the note
            where you put it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Filing />
      </li>

      <li class="step" data-reveal>
        <div class="step-copy">
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <h3>Ask, and AI goes straight to it</h3>
          <p>
            Later, ask AI about it. rotli searches your vault on your computer, and the AI reads only the few notes
            that matter, not the whole vault, so your tokens go to the answer. Secure notes never go to a remote
            model.
          </p>
        </div>
        <AskIndex />
      </li>
    </ol>

    <aside class="llm-wiki" aria-labelledby="llm-wiki-title" data-reveal>
      <h3 id="llm-wiki-title">What is an LLM wiki?</h3>
      <p>
        Plain Markdown notes, kept organized and linked so an AI can build on what you already know instead of
        starting from scratch on every question. Andrej Karpathy described the idea in his{' '}
        <a href={LLM_WIKI_SOURCE} rel="noopener">LLM Wiki note</a> (April 2026), and your rotli vault works the same
        way: you write, and the Librarian adds the areas, summaries, tags, and links.{' '}
        <a href="/blog/getting-started/">Getting started with your vault</a>
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  /* A step: its words on the left, its picture on the right; stacked below 1080px. */
  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(15rem, 21rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 2rem clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }
  .step-copy {
    padding-top: 3.4rem;
  }
  .step-number {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .step-copy h3 {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    font-size: var(--step-h3);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .step-copy p {
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .step {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .step-copy {
      max-width: 38rem;
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }

  /* What is an LLM wiki: a short aside after the story, under one hairline. */
  .llm-wiki {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 5.5rem);
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  .llm-wiki h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .llm-wiki p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .llm-wiki a {
    color: var(--accent-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .llm-wiki a[href^='/'] {
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .llm-wiki a[href^='/']::after {
    content: ' →';
  }

  /* The quokkas hop onto their pictures once, as each step comes in. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    :global(.js) .step:global(.is-visible) :global(.quokka) {
      animation: hop 760ms cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.5, 0.64, 1) 220ms backwards;
      transform-origin: 50% 100%;
    }
  }
  @keyframes hop {
    0% {
      transform: translateY(18px) scale(0.9, 1.08);
    }
    60% {
      transform: translateY(-5px) scale(1, 1);
    }
    80% {
      transform: translateY(0) scale(1.06, 0.93);
    }
  }
</style>
